---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Game from '../components/Game';
import { CREDIT_MILESTONES } from '../lib/credits';
---
<Layout cinema title="Reelillion — The daily movie game · Roll the credits" description="Seven movie questions. Rarer answers roll the credits further. Play Reelillion in a pixel cinema and see if you can reach the post-credits scene.">
  <Game client:load />
  <section class="home-credits-info" aria-labelledby="how-title">
    <p class="eyebrow">THE MOVIE’S OVER. YOUR GAME ISN’T.</p>
    <h2 id="how-title">Stay for the rare answers.</h2>
    <p class="home-intro">A free daily movie game for the films that stayed with you. Seven questions, one movie per answer, and a closing-credit journey powered by your least obvious choices.</p>
    <div class="home-credits-steps">
      <article><span>01 / FIND YOUR FILM</span><h3>Read the question.</h3><p>Name a feature film that fits. You have 20 seconds, or choose Extra time for 40 seconds before starting.</p></article>
      <article><span>02 / GO OFF SCRIPT</span><h3>Make it unexpected.</h3><p>A valid answer scores 10–100 points. The less common the choice, the further your credits roll. No bonus for speed.</p></article>
      <article><span>03 / STAY UNTIL THE END</span><h3>Catch the final scene.</h3><p>Your total out of 700 determines where you finish. Complete the reel with 600 points to unlock a little post-credits surprise.</p></article>
    </div>
    <h3>One score. A whole cast of milestones.</h3>
    <ol class="home-credits-milestones">{CREDIT_MILESTONES.slice(1).map((m,i)=><li><span>{String(i+1).padStart(2,'0')}</span>{m.label}</li>)}</ol>
    <p class="scoring-note">These are signposts in our game’s credits, rather than a ranking of film jobs. Answer rarity starts with Wikipedia views or Wikidata language coverage, then blends in eligible Daily choices. Scores lock when you submit.</p>
    <a class="text-link" href="/how-to-play/">Read the rules and all ten milestones <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
  </section>
  <section class="home-faq"><div><p class="eyebrow">BEFORE THE LIGHTS GO DOWN</p><h2>A few good questions.</h2><p>Free admission. No account.<br/>Just you and your mental movie collection.</p></div><div class="faq-list"><details><summary>What is Reelillion?</summary><p>A daily movie trivia game where you name a film that fits each question. Less obvious valid answers earn more points and roll your credits further through a pixel cinema.</p></details><details><summary>Do I have to wait through real movie credits?</summary><p>No. Each locked answer moves a short, separate credits strip. Your question and controls stay in place, and you start the next question when you’re ready. You can skip the roll, and reduced-motion settings are respected.</p></details><details><summary>What if I spell a title wrong?</summary><p>Small typos, punctuation and common aliases are supported. If a title isn’t in our catalog, you can try again while time remains. A recognized movie that doesn’t fit locks at zero.</p></details><details><summary>When is the next Daily reel?</summary><p>Seven new questions arrive at midnight in New York (America/New_York), including daylight saving changes. Practice and Archive do not affect your Daily score or streak.</p></details><details><summary>How do I unlock the post-credits scene?</summary><p>Finish all seven questions with at least 600 out of 700 points. A perfect 700 unlocks a special version. Every completed reel has its own ending and a spoiler-free result to share.</p></details><details><summary>Are rarity estimates actual player counts?</summary><p>No. Early estimates use Wikipedia pageviews or Wikidata language coverage. Observed eligible player choices are shown separately when available. The source catalog is still growing, and genre classifications can be broad.</p></details></div></section>
</Layout>
